ransliteration":"l-arḍi","verse_key":"2:60"},{"pos":28,"ar":"مُفْسِدِينَ","en_gloss":"spreading corruption","transliteration":"muf'sidīna","verse_key":"2:60"},{"pos":29,"ar":"٦٠","en_gloss":"(60)","transliteration":"","verse_key":"2:60"}]},{"verse_key":"2:61","surah":2,"ayah":61,"ar_uthmani":"وَإِذْ قُلْتُمْ يَـٰمُوسَىٰ لَن نَّصْبِرَ عَلَىٰ طَعَامٍ وَٰحِدٍ فَٱدْعُ لَنَا رَبَّكَ يُخْرِجْ لَنَا مِمَّا تُنۢبِتُ ٱلْأَرْضُ مِنۢ بَقْلِهَا وَقِثَّآئِهَا وَفُومِهَا وَعَدَسِهَا وَبَصَلِهَا ۖ قَالَ أَتَسْتَبْدِلُونَ ٱلَّذِى هُوَ أَدْنَىٰ بِٱلَّذِى هُوَ خَيْرٌ ۚ ٱهْبِطُوا۟ مِصْرًا فَإِنَّ لَكُم مَّا سَأَلْتُمْ ۗ وَضُرِبَتْ عَلَيْهِمُ ٱلذِّلَّةُ وَٱلْمَسْكَنَةُ وَبَآءُو بِغَضَبٍ مِّنَ ٱللَّهِ ۗ ذَٰلِكَ بِأَنَّهُمْ كَانُوا۟ يَكْفُرُونَ بِـَٔايَـٰتِ ٱللَّهِ وَيَقْتُلُونَ ٱلنَّبِيِّـۧنَ بِغَيْرِ ٱلْحَقِّ ۗ ذَٰلِكَ بِمَا عَصَوا۟ وَّكَانُوا۟ يَعْتَدُونَ","en_translation_id":85,"en":"Remember when you said, ‘Moses, we cannot bear to eat only one kind of food, so pray to your Lord to bring out for us some of the earth’s produce, its herbs and cucumbers, its garlic, lentils, and onions.’ He said, ‘Would you exchange better for worse? Go to Egypt and there you will find what you have asked for.’ They were struck with humiliation and wretchedness, and they incurred the wrath of God because they persistently rejected His messages and killed prophets contrary to all that is right. All this was because they disobeyed and were lawbreakers.","words":[{"pos":1,"ar":"وَإِذْ","en_gloss":"And when","transliteration":"wa-idh","verse_key":"2:61"},{"pos":2,"ar":"قُلْتُمْ","en_gloss":"you said","transliteration":"qul'tum","verse_key":"2:61"},{"pos":3,"ar":"يَـٰمُوسَىٰ","en_gloss":"O Musa","transliteration":"yāmūsā","verse_key":"2:61"},{"pos":4,"ar":"لَن","en_gloss":"Never (will)","transliteration":"lan","verse_key":"2:61"},{"pos":5,"ar":"نَّصْبِرَ","en_gloss":"we endure","transliteration":"naṣbira","verse_key":"2:61"},{"pos":6,"ar":"عَلَىٰ","en_gloss":"[on]","transliteration":"ʿalā","verse_key":"2: